  "_about": "Every voiceover voice. ONE list, read by src/lib/tts.ts (server) and src/components/voice-picker.js (browser, fetched from /src/public/voice-catalogue.json). ElevenLabs library voices picked 2026-11-02 from the most-used voices per language and gender (free_users_allowed only); the owner chose Pepper and the London man by ear (Beth was removed 2026-11-13: her ElevenLabs voice came out far quieter and lower quality, about -40 LUFS against Pepper's -22; saved Beth settings now speak as Pepper). `speaker` is the OpenAI voice, used only by a voice with no `elevenlabs` id (no fallback since 2026-11-12). `legacy` voices (the original OpenAI six) stay valid for saved settings but are not offered; since 2026-11-12 each is spoken by an ElevenLabs voice of the same gender (coral, sage, alloy → Pepper; shimmer → Pepper; verse → Archer; onyx → Adam), because OpenAI retires gpt-4o-mini-tts on 6 Jan 2027. Samples: /audio/voices/<id>.mp3, made by scripts/make-voice-samples.mjs. \"wps\": measured words a second (scripts/measure-voice-pace.mjs), used for a long video's word target. A language with a `model` is spoken by that ElevenLabs model with its language_code (Welsh and Norwegian: eleven_multilingual_v2 does not speak them; eleven_v3 does, checked 2026-11-20); every other language uses ELEVENLABS_MODEL. Welsh, Swedish, Danish, Norwegian, Finnish, Greek, Czech and Romanian voices added 2026-11-20 (plan A4): the most-used free library voice per language and gender (Welsh: no Welsh-language voices in the library, so two Welsh-accented voices whose Welsh Scribe heard back word for word).",
